ba91d7858e0ca75037928.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 15 at 6:14PM MDT until August 15 at 6:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 614 PM MDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line\nextending from near Springfield to near Vilas to 11 miles southwest\nof Walsh, moving northeast at 30 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Ping pong ball size hail and 60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect hail\ndamage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect wind\ndamage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nSpringfield, Walsh, Vilas, Two Buttes, and Two Buttes Reservoir.","ends":"2026-08-15T18:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Baca, CO; Prowers, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.11b4fc25f3288404dab5c52c9d6f0fd3a16543db.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.11b4fc25f3288404dab5c52c9d6f0fd3a16543db.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 15 at 5:46PM MDT until August 15 at 6:30PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"SVRPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nSoutheastern Prowers County in southeastern Colorado...\nNorth central Baca County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 630 PM MDT.\n\n* At 546 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Two Buttes,\nor 21 miles northeast of Springfield, moving northeast at 20 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and half dollar size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage\nto roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* This severe thunderstorm will remain over mainly rural areas of\nsoutheastern Prowers and north central Baca Counties.","ends":"2026-08-15T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Baca, CO; Prowers, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8c1c59ef66e1400a93fa2e2fa2bed15ffa134f46.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8c1c59ef66e1400a93fa2e2fa2bed15ffa134f46.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 4:59PM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, east central, and southeast Colorado,\nincluding the following areas, Teller, El Paso, Huerfano, Las\nAnimas, Crowley, Otero, Kiowa, Bent and Prowers Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Abundant monsoon moisture will result in scattered to numerous\nthunderstorms this afternoon and evening which will be capable of\nproducing heavy rainfall and flash flooding, especially for urban\nareas or locations with already saturated soil conditions.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Teller County/Rampart Range above 7500fT/Pike's Peak Between 7500 And 11000 Ft; Pikes Peak above 11000 Ft; Northern El Paso County/Monument Ridge/Rampart Range Below 7500 Ft; Colorado Springs Vicinity/Southern El Paso County/Rampart Range Below 7400 Ft; Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft; Crowley County; La Junta Vicinity/Otero County; Eastern Las Animas County; Western Kiowa County; Eastern Kiowa County; Las Animas Vicinity/Bent County; Lamar Vicinity/Prowers County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 2:05PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM 